# CASM Phase 13 WP81 trusted reference: casmalign1
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmalign1 fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake. NOT produced by CASM. Proves
# .ALIGN's padding computation (boundary - (CasmPc mod boundary)) produces
# correct bytes through the real production parser/emitter (parser.s's
# ppsFillDirective, emit.s's emitAlign/emitAlignMod/emitFillLoop), followed
# by a genuine instruction landing exactly on the resulting boundary.
#
# Source (.ORG $C003, fixed address -- no relocatable symbols involved):
#   .ORG $C003
#   .ALIGN $10    ; pad with default fill value $00 up to the next $10 boundary
#   .BYTE 1
#
# Hand assembly:
#   The load-address header is the .ORG operand itself, $C003, written
#   little-endian as 03 C0 (low byte first).
#   CasmPc starts at $C003. $C003 mod $10 = 3 ($C000 is itself a multiple of
#   $10, and $C003 = $C000+3). Padding = $10 - 3 = $0D (13) bytes of $00.
#   CasmPc after padding = $C003 + $0D = $C010, the next $10 boundary.
#   .BYTE 1 then emits a single byte, $01, at $C010.
#
#   03 C0                                              PRG load-address header ($C003)
#   00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00             .ALIGN $10 (13 zero bytes)
#   01                                                  .BYTE 1
#
# bytes: 16
# sha256: 2f329cdb51f9d25667acab871419ca4226ade5af236406af702d66189a56f50c
# source_sha256: casmalign1.seq=93c3ae15b4320bb568945d21f608e6d84d1e2b5d1faf8d3a4ba1ab99e099970e
# Independent byte derivation reviewed and approved by the user 2026-09-02
#   (WP3 batches 1b-1e -- brain/reviews/2026-09-02-casm-byte-oracle-wp3-batch1bcde-derivations.md).

03 C0
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00
01
